---

### 2. Purpose

Build a self‑service **Dashboard** that lets brick‑and‑mortar business owners claim or add their venue on map.nimiq.com, manage rich profile data, and declare the cryptocurrencies they accept. Complement this with an **Automated Outreach System** that surfaces high‑potential leads and contact details so the Growth team can accelerate merchant onboarding.

---

### 3. Background & Context

- **map.nimiq.com** launched in Jan 2024 as an open, community‑maintained map of crypto‑friendly merchants.
- Manual submissions limit scale and data freshness.
- Google already hosts authoritative venue data. OAuth‑based access to the **Google Business Profile (GBP)** API allows owners to import that data in one click.
- Automated research tools (Perplexity, Grok, Twitter Firehose) can surface promising prospects but need an internal funnel.

---

### 4. Goals & Success Metrics

| Goal                       | Metric                                  | Target (6 months post‑launch) |
| -------------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| Increase verified listings | # of claimed businesses                 | **+2 000**                    |
| Improve data completeness  | Avg. profile completeness score         | **≥ 80 %**                    |
| Boost user trust           | % listings marked accurate by community | **≥ 95 %**                    |
| Outreach efficiency        | Leads converted / Leads contacted       | **≥ 15 %**                    |

---

### 5. Personas

1. **Crypto‑Forward Owner** – runs a café, already accepts BTC/NIM, wants discovery.
2. **Curious Merchant** – considering crypto payments, needs easy setup.
3. **Growth Team Member** – uses dashboard to vet leads and trigger outreach.
4. **End‑User Shopper** – searches map for places that take their coin.

---

### 6. User Stories (MVP)

- *As a business owner*, I can sign in with my **Google account** so I don’t create yet another login.
- *As a signed‑in owner*, I can **import** my Google Business Profile in one click, or **search** if I manage multiple locations.
- *As an owner*, I can **edit** my profile (description, hours, images) and **add which cryptocurrencies** I accept so shoppers have accurate info.
- *As a Growth team member*, I can see an **internal lead list** ranked by potential so I know whom to contact first.
- *As a compliance officer*, I can see an audit trail showing **who edited what & when**.

---

### 7. Functional Requirements

#### 7.1 Authentication & Authorization

| ID     | Requirement                                                             | Priority |
| ------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |
| AUTH‑1 | Support **Google OAuth 2.0 Sign‑In** (Email, Name, GBP scopes)          | Must     |
| AUTH‑2 | Map Google account ↔ merchant record; allow multiple locations per user | Must     |
| AUTH‑3 | Admin role for staff; read‑only mode for Growth users                   | Should   |

#### 7.2 Business Profile Import & Management

| ID    | Requirement                                                                                                                         | Priority |
| ----- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |
| GBP‑1 | Fetch venue data via **Google Business Profile API**: name, address, coordinates, categories, hours, phone, website, photos, rating | Must     |
| GBP‑2 | Provide **search & pick** flow if user manages multiple GBPs                                                                        | Must     |
| GBP‑3 | Allow editing of supplemental fields: *crypto acceptance*, long description, social links                                           | Must     |
| GBP‑4 | Write updates back to internal DB (not to Google) and tag timestamp + editor                                                        | Must     |
| GBP‑5 | 24‑hour **sync job** to refresh ratings & hours from Google                                                                         | Should   |

#### 7.3 Crypto Acceptance Module

| ID       | Requirement                                                     | Priority |
| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |
| CRYPTO‑1 | Multi‑select list of supported coins (BTC, NIM, ETH, SOL, etc.) | Must     |
| CRYPTO‑2 | Option to paste *Lightning / Nimiq PayLink* for future POS flow | Could    |

#### 7.4 Dashboard UX

| ID   | Requirement                                                | Priority |
| ---- | ---------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |
| UI‑1 | Responsive, mobile‑first layout (70 % merchants use phone) | Must     |
| UI‑2 | **Profile completeness meter** with inline tips            | Should   |
| UI‑3 | Search bar with fuzzy match and category filters           | Must     |
| UI‑4 | Map preview showing marker & cluster context               | Should   |

#### 7.5 Automated Outreach System (Growth‑only views)

| ID    | Requirement                                                                                                     | Priority |
| ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |
| OUT‑1 | **Lead collector** cron job: *Perplexity* queries, *Grok* streams, *Twitter* mentions (“we accept crypto here”) | Must     |
| OUT‑2 | Normalize leads → candidate businesses with score (followers, sentiment, category)                              | Should   |
| OUT‑3 | Attempt to auto‑fetch contact details (public email, X DM, website form)                                        | Should   |
| OUT‑4 | Push high‑score leads into CRM (HubSpot) or CSV export                                                          | Could    |

#### 7.6 Data Responsibility & Governance

| ID    | Requirement                                                            | Priority |
| ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |
| GOV‑1 | Display disclaimer: “Owner is responsible for accuracy” before publish | Must     |
| GOV‑2 | Log every change; keep **immutable history** for rollback              | Must     |
| GOV‑3 | GDPR‑compliant data handling; allow deletion requests                  | Must     |

